    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0086",
      "sequence": 98,
      "meaning": "This enchantment lasts for two watches, until Kāma reaches Śambhu. Seeing Śiva, Love becomes apprehensive and the whole world immediately returns to its proper condition; every creature feels relieved, like an intoxicated person when drunkenness passes. Madana fears the formidable, inaccessible Lord Rudra. Ashamed to retreat yet unable to act, he accepts death and devises a plan. At once he manifests lovely spring: rows of newly flowering trees shine, forests, groves, stepwells and ponds become exquisitely beautiful, and love seems to swell everywhere so that even a dead mind would awaken to desire.",
