    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0087",
      "sequence": 99,
      "meaning": "Seeing a fine branch of a mango tree, wrathful Madana climbs it, sets his arrows to the flower-bow, draws to his ear and releases five shafts. They strike Śambhu’s heart; his samādhi breaks and he wakes with unusual agitation. Opening his eyes, the Lord looks in every direction and sees Madana amid fragrant blossoms and leaves. His anger makes the three worlds tremble. Śiva opens his third eye, and at its glance Kāma burns to ash. A great cry rises through the world: the gods are frightened, demons delighted, pleasure-seekers lament their loss of erotic joy, and ascetic practitioners rejoice that their path is unobstructed.",
