    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0088",
      "sequence": 100,
      "meaning": "Śiva assures Rati that when Kṛṣṇa incarnates in the Yadu line to remove earth’s great burden, Kṛṣṇa’s son will become her husband; his word cannot be false. Rati departs. The gods learn what occurred and, with Brahmā and Viṣṇu, go to compassionate Śiva. Each praises him separately; pleased, moon-crested Vṛṣaketu asks why the immortals came. Brahmā says that although Śiva knows every heart, devotion compels the plea: every god ardently wishes to see his wedding with their own eyes.",
