    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0089",
      "sequence": 101,
      "meaning": "The gods ask Śiva to let their eyes feast on that celebration and to do what will humble Kāma’s pride. Burning Kāma and then granting Rati a boon was excellent, for a lord’s nature is first to correct and afterward show grace. Since Pārvatī has performed boundless austerity, he should now accept her. Understanding both Brahmā’s request and Rāma’s command, Śiva happily agrees. The gods beat celestial drums, shower flowers and hail their Lord. Knowing the moment, the Seven Sages arrive; Brahmā sends them at once to Himālaya’s house. They first approach Bhavānī and teasingly say she ignored their advice for Nārada’s teaching, but now her vow is false because Maheśa has burned Kāma.",
